This aircraft is derived from the "x500" simulation model that ships with
PX4-Autopilot (Tools/simulation/gz/models/x500), and carries that model's geometry,
mass, aerodynamic and propulsion data. The meshes are the source model's own,
converted to glTF. The gimbal is the CGO3 from the same collection
(Tools/simulation/gz/models/gimbal, by Stefano Colli, Auterion), the four meshes
converted the same way: the post turns with yaw, the fork with roll, the camera body
with pitch, all about the camera's pitch axis, so the yaw axis sits 16 mm from where
the source model's joint has it. The remesh's lens funnel is covered by a flat bezel
and glass disc of our own, the fork's badge ends are silver, and the meshes are
welded, shaded smooth and textured in PteroSim.

